  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdd offline replay tests for three authentic q08 local-model workflows:\nfinishing, editing the finishing operation, and deleting all operations.\n\n- Add `ReplayTransport` beside the scripted AI-chat tests.\n- Preserve the recorded user messages, replies, call IDs and argument strings.\n- Drive the real panel, parser, inbox, dispatcher and document history.\n- Check the operation values, rendered refusals and one undo group per turn.\n- Check both Allow and Deny for the two recorded native delete calls.\n- Document the fixture format, source mapping and recording procedure.\n\nSource: [q08 recording at its immutable commit](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/tree/d9be74b1408654799446f0e05e2c675fefc619c2/qa/q08/q08-20261122T131017Z).\nAll three fixtures come from `qwen3-coder:latest` on local Ollama,\nCamCraft v0.25.0 (`7e2a8119`). The complete original turns are used.\nThe original raw reply objects match the source transcript exactly.\n\nThe model did not achieve zero stock or the requested 0.2 mm stepdown.\nThe tests assert the actual recorded final parameters. The edit turn deletes\nand re-adds only the finishing operation. It leaves the roughing parameters\nunchanged. Its initial finishing operation is reconstructed from the recorded\n`job-03-after-step3.json` snapshot, not from an invented model reply.\n\nThe historical deletion bypass predates #3424. Replay tests enforce the\ncurrent confirmation policy; they do not recreate the bypass. No production\nparser, tool, policy, CAM, G-code, geometry or simulation behavior changes.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn commit `989aa3878fdce988211c3fd16cd9338ce589fb1d`:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib recorded_q08 -- --nocapture`: 4 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib egui_app::tests::ai_chat -- --nocapture`: 65 passed.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 cargo xtask gate quick --base 903e420b3a6443330233d3e58386d84100a21c5e`: all 10 selected steps passed. The UI library has 1720 passes and 8 existing ignored tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- Focused `rustfmt --check`, local documentation links and `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Source correspondence: metadata, prompts, sessions, steps, every raw reply and usage object match the original transcript.\n- Negative control: temporarily changed the test transport's final `stock_to_leave` argument from 0.1 to 0.7. The finishing test failed on the actual document value, 0.7 versus 0.1. The perturbation was restored; all four tests passed again.\n\nThe complete quick gate used the recorded starting base. Preserved unrelated\nuntracked setup/artifact files appear in its file inventory, but the PR has\nonly ten test/fixture/docs paths. No fixture uses a network transport.\n\n## Exclusions and limitations\n\nNo live inference, model provisioning, traffic capture, GUI application build,\nfull-workspace build, catalog suite, heavy lane or snapshot refresh was run.\nThese tests do not establish physical-machine safety.\n\nThe general review rule requests `gate light`. Its current dry-run selects\nunrelated release builds of `camcraft-motion` and all `camcraft-app` tests.\nThose builds are outside this test-only contribution's authorized scope.\nThe light lane was not run; no light-lane pass is claimed.\n`graphify` is not installed, so its generated graph was not updated.\n\nThis is a contributor pre-check, not a counted upstream collaborator review.\nMaintainer review and merge remain separate.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3411#issuecomment-7208214875\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3411\n",
